{
  "_comment": [
    "Go-vs-Python parity for a ROOT platform file's `tenants:` block (#1982).",
    "Semantics: that block is the platform's per-tenant DEFAULT. The tenant's own",
    "file wins key by key whatever either file is called; a key the tenant file",
    "does not write keeps the platform value; a platform file cannot create a",
    "tenant (no tenant file declares it -> absent on both planes, WARN); a NESTED",
    "platform file's `tenants:` block is read by no plane (exporter WARNs).",
    "Go (config_platform_tenant_overlay_test.go) loads each tree through",
    "NewConfigManager+Load and reads the resolved mysql_connections row (what",
    "/metrics serves); Python (test_platform_tenant_overlay_parity.py) reads the",
    "routing plane, _grar_parse.load_tenant_tree. Neither reads the other's",
    "source; both assert this table.",
    "expect.<tenant>: metric = mysql_connections on /metrics (null = tenant",
    "absent); dedup = routing plane _severity_dedup (null = tenant absent there);",
    "group_wait = routing plane merged group_wait (null = the plane builds no route for it).",
    "exporter_dedup / silent_mode = what the exporter resolves for the tenant",
    "(ResolveSeverityDedup: enable/disable; ResolveSilentModes: sorted target",
    "severities joined by ',', '' = none); null = tenant absent from the exporter.",
    "walker = the walker plane (#2019): /effective (pkg/config ResolveEffective,",
    "also da-guard and the exporter's merged_hash) and describe_tenant.py --show-sources:",
    "{effective_config, platform_overlay}; platform_overlay null = the field is omitted;",
    "walker null = tenant not found. Go asserts metric/exporter_dedup/silent_mode and",
    "walker (and that walker agrees with those three); Python dedup/group_wait and walker.",
    "A tenant file whose FIRST document does not parse declares nothing on either",
    "side (Go: walker parse failure; Python: declared_tenant_ids skips it).",
    "#2326: the routing plane reads the whole tree (ADR-017 amendment 2026-09-28), so a tenant",
    "declared only in a subdirectory has its dedup there too; a nested platform file still adds none.",
    "Measured on main 19dc4c76 before the fix: c1 rows served tx on /metrics;",
    "c3 TX.yaml / 0tx.yaml served 60 (tx.yaml 70); c2-c5 tx.yaml gave dedup",
    "enable (TX.yaml / 0tx.yaml disable).",
    "#2114 rows (numeric / octal-looking / YAML-1.1-bool-looking tenant key):",
    "the tenant id is the key's source TEXT on every plane, so an unquoted",
    "`010:` / `yes:` in the platform file and a quoted one in the tenant file",
    "are one tenant. Each platform block sets `_severity_dedup: disable` so the",
    "Python `dedup` column can see a missed platform value (enable = missed).",
    "#2117 p-rows (profile expansion): the walker plane expands a tenant's",
    "`_profile` exactly as /metrics does (ApplyProfiles): profiles only from ROOT",
    "platform files, fill-in only, precedence tenant file > root platform",
    "`tenants:` entry > profile > defaults chain (subtree carriers included).",
    "walker.profile_overlay = [{profile, file, keys}] (merge order; null = omitted).",
    "The exporter's merged_hash expands it too (the reload contract tests",
    "check every row, p-rows included, against /effective).",
    "Go also checks every `<base>_critical` key of the walker column against the",
    "critical row /metrics serves for <base>. Measured on main 9079583d before",
    "the fix: p1/p2/p3/p6/p7 walker disagreed with /metrics (80 / 70, no",
    "pg_connections_critical).",
    "#2208 tenant_api = the tenant-api merge core (pkg/config MergeTenantWithRootDefaults:",
    "GET /api/v1/tenants/{id}, POST .../validate and the write gate) handed the tenant's",
    "declaring file: the mysql_connections warning row it resolves. null = not reached",
    "(tenant declared by no file, or only by one below the root: tenant-api serves",
    "top-level files). Which top-level file GET opens (confd's filename lookup) is",
    "tenant-api's own and not in this column. Go (config_platform_tenant_overlay_test.go)",
    "asserts it, and that it equals metric except null for a nested tenant. Profiles",
    "are expanded the /metrics way (ApplyProfiles, #1385; p1/p2/p6 served 80 before).",
    "tenant_api is a threshold column only: on platform-metadata-is-never-inherited-or-listed",
    "its 60 is mysql_connections. The core does NOT inherit the platform entry's _metadata",
    "(the walker rule), while /metrics' ResolveMetadata does - a deliberate divergence",
    "pinned by pkg/config TestMergeTenantPlatformLayerMatchesMetrics, not by this table.",
    "#2368 a-rows (#1231 alias spellings): a tree may name metric_key (default",
    "mysql_connections), the threshold its metric / tenant_api columns read; for",
    "mysql_threads_running Go also requires the legacy twin (metric=\"cpu\") to carry",
    "the same value. The tenant file wins per THRESHOLD, not per spelling: a tenant",
    "mysql_cpu beats a platform mysql_threads_running and vice versa, and",
    "platform_overlay names the canonical spelling. The walker effective_config keeps",
    "each layer's own spelling (not canonicalized), so Go reads the legacy spelling",
    "first when checking it against /metrics - sound only because no a-row sets a",
    "legacy spelling in the defaults chain. Measured on main f806e092 before the fix:",
    "a1 served 70 on /metrics and the tenant-api core, walker attributed",
    "mysql_threads_running to _defaults.yaml."
  ],
